  "title": "A Pre-Vote round started while Candidate survives leader establishment; the new Leader starts another election",
  "cause": "The election timer (and trigger().elect(true)) runs pre_elect for a Candidate without cancelling its election; establish_leader does not drop Engine.pre_candidate, and handle_pre_vote_resp calls elect() on quorum without checking the node's role, leaving a stale leader object.",
  "trigger": "A Candidate starts a Pre-Vote round while its real election is in flight; the real election wins, then the Pre-Vote grants arrive.",
  "consequence": "The freshly established Leader steps down and starts an election at term+1 (term inflation, leadership loss); in debug builds RaftCore panics on try_leader_handler's assertion leader.vote >= state.vote.",
  "sites": [
    "openraft/src/core/raft_core.rs:RaftCore::handle_tick_election",
    "openraft/src/engine/engine_impl.rs:Engine::establish_leader",
    "openraft/src/engine/engine_impl.rs:Engine::handle_pre_vote_resp",
    "openraft/src/engine/engine_impl.rs:Engine::try_leader_handler"
  ],
  "actions": [
    "TickElect",
    "ExternalPreElect",
    "HandleVoteResponse",
    "HandlePreVoteResponse"
  ],
  "invariants": [
    "TimerPreVoteElectionFromFollowerState"
  ],
  "premises": [
    "The election timer keeps firing for a Candidate and, with enable_pre_vote, runs pre_elect without cancelling the running election (or an operator calls trigger().elect(true) on a Candidate).",
    "The real election reaches quorum before the Pre-Vote grants are processed (timer path: needs vote replies delayed beyond election_timeout but within the RPC ttl or queued; operator path: no timing constraint)."
  ],
